now to the escalating migration crisis  on the european union's border with  belarus record number of asylum seekers  have been attempting to cross into eu  member state poland in recent days  poland has constructed a border fence  and deployed thousands of soldiers to  turn them back a move that contravenes  international law poland and the eu  accused belarus of manufacturing the  crisis by sending asylum seekers to the  eu's borders a number have already died  of hypothermia or exhaustion and as  temperatures get colder there's no  resolution in sight  from raw in this story let's bring in dw  correspondent jack parock he's at the  border between poland and belarus jack  can you paint us a picture about the  conditions on the ground there  let me just give you a rundown of what  we've just experienced we were informed  that there was an intervention of  perhaps four iraqi migrants about a  kilometer or so down the road behind me  as we drove there uh to try and speak to  these people there was a police block  saying that this was the edge of the  exclusion zone that's a three kilometer  zone away from the border and they said  that we were not able to access those  people that we understood were there  this shows you the difficulty for  transparency and the difficulty for  reporting the situation on the ground we  do know from the polish border  authorities they say that yesterday they  intercepted 605 people which would  indicate that the numbers of people  trying to cross is going up  now jack you've spoken to activists on  the polish side who've witnessed  pushbacks who is behind this  indeed abby we actually just met a local  woman who said that she had been in  contact with a group of iraqi migrants a  family she gave us the phone numbers of  these people after she said she had  given them food and water and tried to  help them in any way she could we've  been in contact uh via messaging with  this family with one of the members of  this family who's on an iraqi dialing  code he sent me a video which was pretty  difficult to watch begging us for help  and saying that they were freezing they  need water holding up a sort of plastic  bottle with dirty water in it there are  three children in that video  we met the woman on the polish side of  the border just on the edge of the  exclusion zone and they dropped us a pin  with their geographic location which  indicated that they are now over the  border in belarus they've also messaged  me just in the last few minutes to say  that they won't try and enter poland  again because they're too tired  this evening we expect it to be like it  was last night bitterly bitterly cold  the situation is very difficult because  the activists don't really know where  where anyone is and they fear  repercussions for their actions in  trying to support people from the polish  government  now dire conditions the weather is not  helping it's going to get colder and now  there's these reports that people in the  border exclusion zone are getting  messages from the polish interior  ministry warning them that belarusian  authorities are trying to poison  migrants  indeed we just got a message again on  our phone  being in the border zone saying do not  cross the polish border and do not take  pills from belarusian soldiers it was  about the same time yesterday we  received that message as well we  understand that those messages started  being delivered the day before we don't  exactly know what that means what the  suggestion is of what the belarusian  soldiers are meant to be  giving to these migrants but clearly  this is a very scary situation for them  as we know there are many families and  as you said we really don't know how  this situation is going to be resolved  we already do know that a number of  people have died in this forest already  during this crisis  dw correspondent jack parak at the  border between poland and belarus thank  you jack  i'm joined now by poland's deputy  foreign minister martin chadduch  minister thank you for taking the time  to speak to dw  thank you very much for having me  as we just said there it appears that  your government is pushing migrants back  from belarus migrants trying to claim  asylum in the european union is that the  case  no it's not the case actually it's an  artificial crisis  orchestrated by the russian regime i  mean  the charter flights has been  set by the belarusian regime all around  the middle east countries  so that the migrants not only asylum  seekers are encouraged somehow to go to  belarus and they're they're being used  as an instrument to destabilize the  eastern european and their boulders  let me just say that those people who  really need an asylum they can apply  for that  at the embassy of poland in iraq or  other countries or any other embassy in  minsk or um or middle east countries  yes it may be an orchestrated crisis as  you say by belarus but it is a crisis  nonetheless and we have our  correspondent there he's in the border  region right now and he says he's spoken  to activists on the polish side who've  witnessed these pushbacks and he's in  touch with migrants on the belarussian  side who say they were in poland but  were taken back across the border that's  illegal  well um  depends what what do you mean by saying  illegal according to what i mean the  geneva convention states that their  people shouldn't be pushed back to the  country where they came from when where  they are in danger so we are not pushing  back those people to um syria or i don't  know afghanistan they came legally to  belarus so sometimes of course the  redirector redirecting having in mind  the information that they are not in  germany because they really want to go  to germany mostly that's what they ask  us to do we want to go to germany to get  the asylum there once they are informed  that it's not germany they sometimes  they they decide by themselves to go  back to belarus to try the other or the  other way uh or they are just somehow  blocked by the polish  board guards do not enter the polish  territory because it's illegal if you  want to get to the polish territory then  you have to go to the crossing point  with the special documents with the visa  minister are you saying then if these  migrants have actually made it on to  polish soil that they are not being  pushed back by your officials  well uh what do you mean by saying push  backs there are i mean there are  informed that they are on the territory  of poland not german not germany  if they want to apply for asylum in in  in germany then it's not the way to do  on the polish territory so some of them  they do really decide to go back to um  to belarus the others  are informed that this is illegal what  they've done so they need to go on their  back but  if i may now of course we can discuss  about this procedure but  i think we should have in mind that it  is an orchestrated a hybrid attack um  by the russian regime that he has  invited those migrants to destabilize us  and as a revenge to our policy towards i  mean our european policy towards belarus  because when okasenka announced publicly  the possible migration crisis on the on  the border on the that very day when we  as the european union 27 countries  decided to sanction him him and the and  and the russian regime so it is a kind  of  revenge uh where the people are  instrumentalized by by lukashenko  minister i do want to ask you a little  bit more about belarus um  there's that border exclusion zone that  your government has set up and people  who are in that area appear to be  receiving messages that belarusian  authorities are trying to poison  migrants the same warning is on your  interior ministries website i'm just  going to read it there it says do not  take any pills or medication given to  you in belarus you may be poisoned  what evidence does poland have the  balleris is doing this  well we do have testimonies of those  migrants found already on the polish  side some of them um  told us that they were offered by the uh  by some of the the kgb officers with uh  special pills uh that was at the quite  at the very beginning of this crisis  when mr wukashenka wanted to attract the  interests of media  around this crisis so we found some deaf  corpse  on the  at the border that it was very probable  that some of them  were poisoned that's why we appeal to  those people do not take any any pills  from from them  i'd like to move on now there are  concerns that your country uh might be  going through at potentially a poll exit  the so-called poll exit we saw over the  weekend over a hundred thousand people  gather in the capitol there to show  their support for being in the european  union  and this was in reaction to the protest  about the polish constitutional court  ruling that national law supersedes eu  law is your government going down a path  towards a poll exit  not at all  we are a member of the eu are we going  to stay in the in the eu  eu  and i mean eu is a natural environment  for me for poland so nothing like that  of course there was a demonstration um  orchestrated by donald tusk by the  opposition leader more or less to  support him as the opposition leader  with a kind of fake argument that there  is a possible policy there is nothing  like this 90 percent of polls are um  there are i mean they do support our  membership  in the eu and also the government  supports our membership but of course  the constitutional tribunal just like  the federal tribunal constitution  tribunal in castro germany or  the same with the in the french case um  they said that the most important  law or legislation in poland in in our  countries is the constitution of poland  or um in case of germany or france the  same and that  we accept the eu regulations those which  are based on the eu treaties but those  uh regulations uh which are um written  in the polish constitutions um we do  also i'm somehow obliged to um to  observe those regulations i mean there  are competences of the eu and there are  competences of the member  member states  and let's keep it as it is  marcin  polish deputy foreign minister minister  thank you for taking the time to speak  with dw we appreciate it thank you very  much  thank you  you

